Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 18:01:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] fix(ops): app loggers at INFO; idempotent scheduler
 shutdown

Found by booting the real 2-worker uvicorn stack during the Phase 0-2
review:

- The root logger is pinned at WARNING (to keep third-party libraries
  quiet), so the "This worker is now the scheduler leader" line and every
  other INFO message from app.* was silently dropped. Add
  configure_app_log_level() driven by APP_LOG_LEVEL (default INFO) that
  raises only the application namespaces, leaving root untouched.
- On every worker exit the leader's on_release callback and the lifespan
  both called stop_scheduler() in the same tick; AsyncIOScheduler defers
  shutdown to the loop so `running` was still True and the second call
  raised SchedulerNotRunningError. stop_scheduler() is now idempotent.

Verified: leader line logged exactly once across 2 workers, SIGTERM
shutdown has no tracebacks, /ready 200.

